+cff-version: 1.2.0
+message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
+title: "Intelligence Regulation: zero-knowledge proofs of LLM inference"
+type: software
+authors:
+  - family-names: Rielly
+    given-names: Victor
+# repository-code: <REPOSITORY URL: pending Victor (repository name not ruled)>
+# version / date-released: set at the v0.1.0 tag
+license:
+  - MIT
+  - Apache-2.0
+abstract: >-
+  A research prototype of zero-knowledge proofs that a public-weight language model
+  computed a stated result while its input, output and intermediate activations stay
+  hidden. It includes a hash-based prover over the Goldilocks field (token round 16b
+  reference) with proofs of a Shieldstral-1.0-3B classifier verdict and of TinyLlama-1.1B
+  and Llama-3-8B next tokens, a RISC Zero zkVM route with Groth16 receipts, the privacy-gate
+  analysis tools, and the design, review and decision records.
+keywords:
+  - zero-knowledge proofs
+  - verifiable inference
+  - large language models
+  - sumcheck
+  - lookup arguments
+  - Goldilocks field
