+## 5. Check a published receipt
+
+The intended path is listed below. It is not yet self-service (see section 3).
+
+1. Fetch the model at its pinned revision and check every file against its pin.
+   Shieldstral-1.0-3B is revision `003ec7e2…`, about 7.7 GB; the pins are in
+   `evidence/zk60_shieldstral_prep_20261021/`. Shieldstral is distributed by Mistral AI
+   under Apache-2.0 behind an access form, so it is not mirrored here.
+2. Rebuild the integer export with `tools/model-export/shieldstral-export/`.
+3. Build `zk60_classify` with
+   `cargo build --release --locked --manifest-path hashline/Cargo.toml --example zk60_classify`.
+   Its digest will differ from the development binary `dfb8025e…`, because the build
+   path is compiled in.
+4. Run `zk60_classify verify` on the receipt directory with the verifier copy of the
+   export. `evidence/zk60_token_io_r1_20261017/cli/README.md` describes the command
+   and the statement schema.
+
+The receipts of the first real post (84 public segments, 2.55 GB) are not in this
+repository. They are intended as release assets with a `SHA256SUMS` file.
