+# Security policy
+
+## Status
+
+This is a **research prototype**. Nothing in it has had an external security audit.
+Do not use it to protect real data, money or safety decisions.
+
+What has been done:
+- internal adversarial reviews, by AI agents and the author;
+- recorded soundness counts (`docs/zkmatrix-poc/SOUNDNESS_REFERENCE.md`);
+- a privacy-gate analysis (`privacy-gate/`).
+
+Every ruling, including each accepted deviation, is in
+`docs/zkmatrix-poc/ZK60_DECISIONS.md`. Read it before relying on any property.
+
+The deviations a user must know:
+- **zkVM route:** about 97 bits of conjectured soundness (D3) and a Groth16 trusted
+  setup (D4).
+- **Hash-based prover (`hashline`):** whole-run soundness floors of about 95 to 97 bits,
+  depending on the profile, as counted in the reviews.
+- **Privacy:** accepted only for the named TinyLlama-1.1B 32-token artifacts (D33, D36).
+  The classifier's privacy statement is still a draft.
+- **Leakage:** timing, memory and power are out of scope (D20). The input length is
+  public for classifier proofs (D45).
+
+## Reporting a vulnerability
+
+Please report soundness bugs (a false statement that verifies), privacy leaks (a proof
+or its side channels revealing hidden data) and verifier crashes **privately**:
+
+- through GitHub's private vulnerability reporting ("Report a vulnerability" on the
+  repository's Security tab), once the repository is public; or
+- by email: <CONTACT: pending Victor>
+
+Please include:
+- the commit or release;
+- the profile and command;
+- a minimal reproducer, if you have one;
+- whether you have told anyone else.
+
+Do not open a public issue for an unfixed vulnerability. This is a research project,
+so there is no bounty and no guaranteed response time. Confirmed findings are credited
+in the decisions register and the release notes, unless you ask otherwise.
+
+## Scope
+
+In scope:
+- `hashline/` and `zkp-core/`: the prover, the verifier and the transcript;
+- the zkVM route (`zkvm-*`);
+- `privacy-gate/`;
+- the published receipt formats.
+
+Out of scope:
+- the demo app's testnet deployment;
+- third-party dependencies (report those upstream);
+- the security of any model's outputs.
